From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the console cursor stays in a confining window

A game or VM viewer confines the pointer to its window, or part of it,
through zwp_pointer_constraints_v1, and the shell passes that on as
boxes. OzonePlatform::SetDomicilePointerConfinement holds the DRM cursor
inside them: DrmCursor clamps each mouse and tablet move with
ConfinedMove (ui/ozone/platform/drm/domicile/drm_pointer_confinement.h),
which works in the confining window's pixels, so a box that reaches
across a seam holds the pointer on both monitors. Warps are not held.
Other platforms answer false: nested, the host compositor moves the
pointer, and headless, the compositor does. The control channel's
ConfinePointer reaches domicile::ConfinePointerIn through the binder,
as a warp reaches WarpPointerIn.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
